On Jul 21, 5:38 pm, bl...@kingdomrpg.com wrote:
>    Are artifacts safely enchantable at +5, like elven stuff? My wizard-
> mode tests say yes. Better yet, is that online source code listing
> still up so I can see for myself. (Not that I'm paranoid or anything.)

Enchanting weapons is not the same as enchanting armor. All weapons <=
+5 can be safely enchanted. As various spoilers point out, if you have
extra scrolls to go around, it may be worthwhile to remove a point of
enchantment from a +6 weapon (with a cursed scroll of enchant weapon)
in order to have another chance at safely enchanting it to +7.

You can continue to enchant weapons of +6 or higher, but there is a
2/3 probability that they will be vaporized, artifacts included.

I think it would be nice if the RNG occasionally coughed up ordinary
weapons enchanted to higher values than +7, but I'm not sure whether
it can or does.



